  "about": {
   "version": "1.0",
   "description": "The whole Earth in one bit, after Google Earth: drag to turn the globe, scroll to come down to it, and fly anywhere from the Go menu. The Sun lights it as it does now, or at any hour the Time menu turns to, against the real stars, and Go flies Apollo 8's free return to the Moon and back, condensed or in real time. Imagery from NASA's Blue Marble; coastlines and borders from Natural Earth; stars from the Yale Bright Star Catalogue."
